# Mistake in `libsv/libsv/coders/encoder_8b10b.sv`

- Source URL: https://github.com/bensampson5/libsv/issues/151

Hello!

I am working on implementing 8b/10b encoding in a different project, and I stumbled upon the lookup table for encoding in this project. After writing my tests, I think I have found a mistake in your code in [encoder_8b10b.sv](https://github.com/bensampson5/libsv/blob/main/libsv/coders/encoder_8b10b.sv): for all code groups D28.X, the last 6 bits are `001110` while they should actually be `011100` according to the table in IEEE 802.3. Could this be possible?

